    1. Pick grid size H in [14,17], W in [18,19], bg=0, fg=random non-zero color
    2. Pick N in [4,5]. Pick common_holes in [1,4]. Pick unique_holes in [1,4] where unique_holes != common_holes
    3. Generate N-1 blocks with common_holes each and 1 block with unique_holes, placing holes at random non-center interior positions with no two holes 4-adjacent
    4. Place all N blocks on the grid with Chebyshev gap >= 1 between any pair of bboxes; blocks may extend to grid edges; use rejection sampling or greedy placement
    5. Output is the crop of the unique block
```
