<description>
Stamp translated copies of a monochrome template guided by a singleton pixel layout.

Input structure:
- bg = background. A large monochrome shape (template, color T).
- Singleton pixels elsewhere: exactly one is color T (layout origin); the rest share color O (overlap color).
- Singletons sit on a uniform-spacing lattice.

Rule:
- Convert each singleton's offset from the origin into coarse lattice units.
- Place a template copy at each offset, scaled by template height/width.
- The origin's copy is painted O instead of T.
- Any pixel covered by two or more copies is also recolored to O.

Key insight: The single T-colored singleton identifies both the origin position and the "self" copy, which is uniquely recolored.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "marker pixel set s with different colored center pixel and peripheral pixels",
  "dst": "monochrome sprite d",
  "match_cond": "s.center.color == d.color",
  "transform": "s.peripheral_pixels -> d. d.color -> s.peripheral_pixels.color"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 22x22, single bg color
  colors: 3 distinct colors -- bg, T (template), O (overlap); all from 0-9
  template (dst):
    monochrome sprite, color T, 4-connected single component
    bbox: 3-4 rows x 3 cols; area 6-10; fill ratio 0.65-0.85
    both first and last row of bbox contain >=1 filled cell; same for cols
  singletons (src lattice):
    count: 5-6 (exactly 1 origin colored T, rest 4-5 colored O)
    uniform spacing: gunit = 2 [observed]
    lattice pattern: 4-connected polyomino of 5-6 cells on integer grid
    lattice extent: 3-4 unit rows x 3-4 unit cols
    origin (0,0): strictly interior -- never at min/max row or col of lattice bbox
  placement:
    template and singleton-cluster bboxes are disjoint, separated by >=1 bg cell
  output:
    stamp template at each lattice delta scaled by (h, w) from template bbox origin
    origin copy painted O; all other copies painted T
    no pixel overlap between stamps in eval data [observed]
    all stamps fit fully inside 22x22 grid
    singletons removed; original template overwritten by origin stamp (color O)

generation_strategy:
  output-first approach:
  1. Pick bg, T, O as 3 distinct colors.
  2. Build template in h x w bbox (h in {3,4}, w=3): random 4-connected shape, area 6-10, touching all bbox edges.
  3. Build lattice polyomino: 5-6 cells on integer grid, 4-connected, extent 3-4 x 3-4. Designate one strictly-interior cell as origin.
  4. Place template bbox at (r0,c0) so all stamps (r0+dr*h, c0+dc*w) fit in 22x22.
  5. Verify no pixel overlap between adjacent stamps (template is sparse enough).
  6. Pick singleton origin (orr,orc) with gunit=2 so all singleton positions fit in grid and cluster bbox is disjoint from template bbox.
  7. Input = bg grid + template at bbox (color T) + singletons (origin=T, others=O).
